## Context
Ticket 1196 (PR #1800) exports GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-agent through scripts/bash-env.sh, which only Claude Code
shells load (BASH_ENV in Claude settings). Codex and Pi shells still run gh as the owner login, so the 1196 guarantee
(no session credential can edit rulesets or settings) holds for one runtime of three.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Codex and Pi agent shells resolve gh to the agent config when ~/.config/gh-agent/hosts.yml exists; the
      author's interactive shell does not.
- [ ] A ruleset write from each runtime's agent shell returns 403 (measured once per runtime, logged).
- [ ] conception/local-merge-gate-policy.md's Session credential section drops the gap; the harness gate passes.

Related: [[1196]].

## Imagine (raid 2026-10-27b)
- Premise check: holds. scripts/bash-env.sh:60-ish exports GH_CONFIG_DIR; BASH_ENV is wired only in the claude
  branch of adapters/lifecycle.py (~l.385-390) and projections.json lists bash-env.sh for runtime "claude" only.
  Codex and Pi have no shell-env hook (hooks.json = SessionStart + PreToolUse guard; idh-guard.ts = guard only).
  Nothing merged on these surfaces since 2026-10-27 creation (git log clean on shell-init.sh, lifecycle.py, adapters).
- Simplest path: scripts/shell-init.sh already wraps `codex` and `pi` (same file the author's bashrc sources, but the
  wrappers only affect the launched child). Add one helper `_idh_agent_gh` that, when GH_CONFIG_DIR is unset and
  $HOME/.config/gh-agent/hosts.yml exists, makes the launch run as `GH_CONFIG_DIR=... command codex "$@"`
  (env-prefix on the command, no export, so the author's interactive shell never gets it). Child shells inherit it
  (Codex shell_environment_policy default inherits all; GH_CONFIG_DIR is not KEY/SECRET/TOKEN-named; to be measured).
  YAGNI: no new Pi extension env injection, no projection entry, no new loader. Alternatives rejected: extending
  BASH_ENV to codex/pi (not honoured by their shell spawn, unproven; also loads .env parse into those runtimes);
  Codex config.toml set (per-user file outside the harness, drift).
  Known gap, state it in the policy: launches outside the wrappers (IDE extension, desktop app, cron) stay on the owner login.
- Risk class: concrete fix with one measurement-dependent point (does the env reach each runtime's tool shell).
  Coder: sonnet.

## Plan
1. scripts/shell-init.sh: add `_idh_agent_gh_env` (prints nothing; returns 0 when hosts.yml exists and
   GH_CONFIG_DIR unset). In `codex` and `pi` use `env GH_CONFIG_DIR="$HOME/.config/gh-agent" command codex "$@"`
   in that case, else plain `command`. Leave `claude` alone (BASH_ENV handles it).
2. tests/test_shell_init_gh_agent.sh (model on tests/test_bash_env_gh_agent_config.sh): hermetic HOME, stub `codex`/`pi`
   on PATH that print $GH_CONFIG_DIR, source shell-init with IDH_SKIP_VALIDATE=1; cases: config present -> path;
   hosts.yml missing -> unset; caller-set GH_CONFIG_DIR wins; parent shell afterwards still has GH_CONFIG_DIR unset
   (author's shell unaffected); `claude` wrapper untouched.
3. conception/local-merge-gate-policy.md Session credential: replace the "Loader coverage" bullet with the
   wrapper mechanism, the measured 403 per runtime, and the residual non-wrapper-launch gap. Update STATE.md
   Handoff line "Codex and Pi shells do not load it yet" only if the coder's PR lands (orchestrator may do it at wrap-up).
4. Measurement (exit 2): run `codex exec` and `pi --print` under the wrappers, each asking its bash tool to run
   `gh api -X POST repos/<owner>/<repo>/rulesets` with an invalid-empty body (expect 403 before validation);
   also `gh api user --jq .login` to show the identity. Log both outputs in the PR body / policy doc. Needs live
   model calls and the padme token: a sonnet coder on padme can do it; if a runtime is unreachable, the coder
   reports "unmeasured: <reason>", leaves the box unchecked, and no null is claimed.
- First test: step 2 case "config present" asserts the stub child sees the exact gh-agent path AND the parent does not.
  A wrong implementation that `export`s in the wrapper passes the first half but fails the parent-clean assertion;
  one that skips the hosts.yml check fails the missing-config case. Stubs prove env passing, not that the real
  runtimes forward it: that is step 4.
- Files touched: scripts/shell-init.sh, tests/test_shell_init_gh_agent.sh (new), conception/local-merge-gate-policy.md,
  maybe STATE.md. Registries: none (tests glob-discovered? coder confirms the .sh runner picks it up; no
  allowlist expected). Check tests/test_skill_seam.py and tests/test_projection_validator.py still pass (they source shell-init).
- Dependencies: none open; 1196 merged. File overlap: 1285 (notes refs protection) edits the same policy doc,
  different bullet ("Limitation"); keep in separate waves or accept a trivial rebase.
- Exit mapping: EC1 -> steps 1-2 (+ step 4 shows real runtimes). EC2 -> step 4 (live; coder reports, cannot be a unit test).
  EC3 -> step 3, then `make` gate / doc check named in the repo gate.

## Orchestrator decisions (raid 2026-10-27b)
- The live 403 probe must use a deliberately invalid ruleset body (e.g. an empty JSON object), so a shell that wrongly carries owner rights gets 422 and nothing is created. Never send a valid ruleset. A runtime that cannot be driven headless on padme is reported 'unmeasured', not a pass.

## Feasibility (raid 2026-10-27b)
PASS: wrappers at scripts/shell-init.sh:89/95; tests/test_bash_suites.py globs test_*.sh. codex/pi must be logged in for the live probe, else 'unmeasured'. STATE.md left to the orchestrator. Wave 1.
